#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100578 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Sine Function"}] :question/id #uuid "48da9a24-92e2-5b0c-a92e-65fa2a81ff4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3779" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(4x-90^\\circ\\right)} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-{90}^{∘} & =-{30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n, & \\, & \\, & 4x-{90}^{∘} & =-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & ={90}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 4x & ={90}^{∘}-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ 4x & ={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 4x & =-{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+{90}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & x & =-{15}^{∘}+{90}^{∘}n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100579 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "857ee3a0-9f63-531c-a06c-285e67846f0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-3780" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(2x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} \\right) =  -1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100580 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "0d83d1d9-82cc-5d34-a335-1f49fbabd194" :question/math-academy-id "e-3781" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\sec\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sqrt{2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n, \\qquad\\qquad 2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{7\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ 2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x=-\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & x=\\frac{5\\pi }{8}+\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100707 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ac0a989f-8766-5650-a388-f81206fe76ab" :question/math-academy-id "e-8659" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\cos \\left(6x + 75^\\circ \\right) = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+{75}^{∘} & ={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 6x+{75}^{∘} & ={225}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 6x & ={150}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={25}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4eac346-ac15-5c4d-9a98-d37ff9fca2b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279311} {:answer/id #uuid "07130973-fe51-567d-aefd-749ce7d301d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279312} {:answer/id #uuid "45a4beb0-ea67-5646-9d68-45fcfebf527c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279313} {:answer/id #uuid "17d84f83-880b-5c5f-ae0c-b5350fd04a40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279314} {:answer/id #uuid "d55c285c-019b-5e94-b08c-3a62bac8bad5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d55c285c-019b-5e94-b08c-3a62bac8bad5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279315} :answer-field/id #uuid "349bcaa5-674e-50d6-beab-5215985552c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b76b907c-4182-5eef-ac99-2d356340ad89" :question/math-academy-id "q-121064" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $n$ is any integer. What could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{9}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{9}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279316 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f63b9c6-8b22-55d3-9f1c-655f92571064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "270" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279318} {:answer/id #uuid "d9dfaab9-8548-5173-9971-c29f6d1de9f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279319} {:answer/id #uuid "6fa20bed-c0ee-5160-9cb3-f04fe3d0f927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279320} {:answer/id #uuid "3a481257-67ca-5aba-811f-7131c8a0cea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279321} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d32859-686c-5df3-a522-9dcec0ca38e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9dfaab9-8548-5173-9971-c29f6d1de9f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279319} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d88ec9b-a5c6-5f52-b55a-3f23e591225c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e2a4d635-4370-5450-961f-de86ce3806b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-121068" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=-2.\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx={a}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x={480}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}={120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,\\frac{x}{2}={240}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & ={120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,\\frac{x}{2} & ={240}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={240}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,x & ={480}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=240.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279323 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f531d1ab-646b-50c9-9dd6-64907eef1f71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279325} {:answer/id #uuid "2df6e8df-3e7e-50d4-9019-054f1b4765b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279326} {:answer/id #uuid "0096e992-63ab-5731-ab9a-4ae0e332eeb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279327} {:answer/id #uuid "d3932372-9171-5f70-8c8f-316868ba95c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279328} {:answer/id #uuid "4e899ce5-e583-53a1-827e-7429bf319bfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0096e992-63ab-5731-ab9a-4ae0e332eeb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279327} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecd6b3ae-8526-5334-a9aa-490618f27f79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9a968c79-5a9b-586d-b119-90ef0b955726" :question/math-academy-id "q-121076" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(5x)=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5},\\,x=a+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n5x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n,\\,5x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n, & \\,5x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5}, & \\,x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{30}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=\\frac{7\\pi }{30}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74ceac17-f52a-5863-a5bc-044723ffc88a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279332} {:answer/id #uuid "07a7fb6d-1b22-52ba-8f3f-0daeae266d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{165}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279333} {:answer/id #uuid "9c2d6eb0-cfd4-5363-bf0f-0efb712803f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279334} {:answer/id #uuid "914ab5c3-d6c3-5b42-a5ca-0d4df6aba908" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{105}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279335} {:answer/id #uuid "2302743b-5b29-596b-b8db-d3a6329ac0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{55}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2302743b-5b29-596b-b8db-d3a6329ac0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{55}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279336} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a4cb5c-fa4e-589c-b04a-84cce117001e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9654a1b-7cb1-5764-826b-bc9327f43dc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-16252" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{30}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=-{25}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}n,\\,x=b+{120}^{∘}n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $b?$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+{30}^{∘} & =-{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n, & \\, & \\, & 3x+{30}^{∘} & =-{135}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-{30}^{∘}-{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 3x & =-{30}^{∘}-{135}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ 3x & =-{75}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 3x & =-{165}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ x & =-{25}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & x & =-{55}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b=-{55}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c638b96-47ee-5f46-bd44-e2c319c9a92c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279339} {:answer/id #uuid "4a281838-b650-5d7a-81e1-369454da05c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279340} {:answer/id #uuid "c72fc158-c62f-5859-b51a-0b958312cf48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279341} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdba6e8-ea8d-5059-a95f-ad1822f3f0c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279342} {:answer/id #uuid "2a78bf9c-d026-5c91-a854-d7de279eb858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a281838-b650-5d7a-81e1-369454da05c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279340} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3e97244-04e6-5e47-8935-61b43a64a204" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1cbccf1-b507-517b-abb8-d47cd6541c32" :question/math-academy-id "q-19756" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=1\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=\\pi a+\\pi n\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+\\frac{3\\pi }{4} & =0+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{8}+\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-\\frac{3}{8}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279344 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0706ddf7-1823-5bc2-ab3f-bf282c0c2abc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0706ddf7-1823-5bc2-ab3f-bf282c0c2abc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279346} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ae08936-817a-5f84-b398-1a2d05fa013f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66dce54a-8cfe-5e60-a256-10588f9ab244" :question/math-academy-id "q-274647" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=\\pi +2\\pi n,\\,x=b\\pi +2\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[0,2).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{4\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{6\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\pi +2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b=\\frac{3}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279347 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75185d75-f5d4-5ffb-9d27-aba442321528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75185d75-f5d4-5ffb-9d27-aba442321528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279349} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f10820-c2b3-54b6-9b01-4fc2a979bbae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b3cf854f-327f-5c34-bbfc-5fd91da61753" :question/math-academy-id "q-327876" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-{60}^{∘})=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=b+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x={195}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{60}^{∘} & ={210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 2x-{60}^{∘} & ={330}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={210}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={330}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 2x & ={270}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={390}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={135}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={195}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b={135}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f74355d-ff69-5e27-a515-2a5fd8f55d67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f74355d-ff69-5e27-a515-2a5fd8f55d67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279352} :answer-field/id #uuid "da6c17b7-c1e2-563b-aa55-a2edef18d467" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ff48e49-1d81-5ee1-b181-e43dce476999" :question/math-academy-id "q-328237" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{125}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=-{40}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{125}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 2x+{125}^{∘} & ={315}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}-{125}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={315}^{∘}-{125}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 2x & =-{80}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={190}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & =-{40}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={95}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={95}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99b0beee-b0fa-53d0-a2ce-030d3810209c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99b0beee-b0fa-53d0-a2ce-030d3810209c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279355} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8fbf220-6b4b-525a-acbd-ef5e1b674642" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9437a79-2002-51b0-8bf3-405d6098af03" :question/math-academy-id "q-328240" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+{50}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=a+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x={175}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $({0}^{∘},{90}^{∘}].$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+{50}^{∘} & ={135}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & x+{50}^{∘} & ={225}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={135}^{∘}-{50}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={225}^{∘}-{50}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={85}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={175}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={85}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a17142ab-c730-52e5-8620-e381e5845f4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279358} {:answer/id #uuid "1da1f529-a671-555a-85cc-177b012525e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1da1f529-a671-555a-85cc-177b012525e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279359} :answer-field/id #uuid "e06ffba9-32a2-5216-b5d7-09ac7ed767e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c742ee53-0710-5915-b4de-a43b4cebec18" :question/math-academy-id "q-328241" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+{150}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx={720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}+{150}^{∘} & ={150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2}+{150}^{∘} & ={210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & ={150}^{∘}-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2} & ={210}^{∘}-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & ={360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2} & ={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={720}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={120}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={120}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a533e69-4803-510e-a5a4-f64179585cb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279362} {:answer/id #uuid "59c4bb4b-5d88-561a-b814-a21b05f8d3a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a533e69-4803-510e-a5a4-f64179585cb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279362} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba0bdefe-45bc-59ec-a82c-9194b0659243" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c86bceb5-09a7-500b-b424-00e8e45afd90" :question/math-academy-id "q-328250" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{30}^{∘})=1\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a+n\\cdot {90}^{∘},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{90}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{30}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & ={75}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={37.5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=37.5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e6e6c86-19b5-5ec4-8709-587ec4eda889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279366} {:answer/id #uuid "b94c29a2-a684-585b-9732-b32947eaf8ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e6e6c86-19b5-5ec4-8709-587ec4eda889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279366} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ff6a574-745c-5e34-989b-ef8731d3e884" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba4307cd-dbfa-5f5c-927a-c736896cca91" :question/math-academy-id "q-328425" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x+{30}^{∘})=0\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a+n\\cdot {45}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{45}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x+{30}^{∘})=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+{30}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & ={90}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 4x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+n\\cdot {45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={15}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92601dc4-0050-5a19-b9f0-fc73ccb31553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92601dc4-0050-5a19-b9f0-fc73ccb31553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279370} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b5e88a9-c874-5ca0-b627-764f9f21763b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49b2ee85-1a6f-5f10-affa-73f92f4121c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-328434" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-1\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +2n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[0,2).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=\\frac{1}{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8184fa4-8e05-5b4d-a609-a70179503aca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8184fa4-8e05-5b4d-a609-a70179503aca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279373} :answer-field/id #uuid "0572e39f-2d80-5b82-869f-695d5035edc6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "67ae8131-8848-5415-a2f6-cec00ad3c84e" :question/math-academy-id "q-328452" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(3x)=-2\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2\\pi }{9}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{3},\\,x=a\\pi +\\frac{2\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[0,\\frac{2}{3}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n3x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n,\\,3x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n, & \\,3x & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{9}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{3}, & \\,x & =\\frac{4\\pi }{9}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=\\frac{4}{9}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279374 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc05165d-ad81-500b-b846-1dc45f03a177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc05165d-ad81-500b-b846-1dc45f03a177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279376} :answer-field/id #uuid "40693c9f-68a2-5c18-9307-28072c764274" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f8fdd777-5df8-5c21-87ef-46d12c5520f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-330218" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{120}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=-{45}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{120}^{∘} & ={30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 2x+{120}^{∘} & ={330}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={30}^{∘}-{120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={330}^{∘}-{120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 2x & =-{90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & =-{45}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={105}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={105}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb19f87d-1e4d-5313-ae6f-2ecb7fa8b53a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279379} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b615d0-81b8-5c45-b243-fae76c4c682f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0b615d0-81b8-5c45-b243-fae76c4c682f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279380} :answer-field/id #uuid "46a10090-99e8-5dbe-8438-8f682dc56fe8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "98a70c61-b70c-50f6-869d-66013f377908" :question/math-academy-id "q-331954" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-{45}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx={15}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=b+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{72}^{∘}).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-{45}^{∘} & ={30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 5x-{45}^{∘} & ={150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & ={30}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={150}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 5x & ={75}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={195}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={39}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b={39}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f3212f7-2bbb-57b8-989b-fea88f88eb35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099517} {:answer/id #uuid "09faa734-92ee-567c-b20b-7a2dffc50718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099518} {:answer/id #uuid "0a6a0152-99a7-568c-a9a4-bee833e70c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099519} {:answer/id #uuid "0b7348e7-7606-5fe7-a1af-d3aea2703612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "210" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099520} {:answer/id #uuid "570cc21b-9087-50e4-9da7-f38c0f5bb041" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a6a0152-99a7-568c-a9a4-bee833e70c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099519} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ea3b4b7-d26a-533c-8b3c-d836bed86da8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d1cd618-3e37-5bc5-a865-78591e0eea79" :question/math-academy-id "q-42788" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘})=2.\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx={a}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=1\\,{120}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘}={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘}={300}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{4}=-{20}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,\\frac{x}{4}=-{20}^{∘}+{300}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ \\frac{x}{4}={40}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,\\frac{x}{4}={280}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x={160}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,x=1\\,{120}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=160.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3ef9952-18b2-58f7-85f8-0f072bfa89eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099523} {:answer/id #uuid "d67415c6-71ee-5b67-8e0d-760ba6936c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5π}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099524} {:answer/id #uuid "13b70d9b-a3d1-5d67-8aac-995a284d08b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7π}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099525} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6b0c63-e3e2-5a6d-93d3-daec6e69f03c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099526} {:answer/id #uuid "6b032a6b-ce11-5356-9e27-024c3b6892ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13b70d9b-a3d1-5d67-8aac-995a284d08b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7π}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099525} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c7da5f-c824-5006-92f3-48ac4254f60a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bd51b773-7114-5c60-8ae3-bd4c43f5e27a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42789" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric  equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡2x=-2\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a+\\pi n,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}+\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}+n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}+n\\pi \\,\\,\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eee3248c-0075-5099-b617-4bce0d6f5717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279383} {:answer/id #uuid "6181be44-4b76-5745-86b9-4ac35f4a7823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279384} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2076ec-aa51-5038-9de8-b30d4b8869a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279385} {:answer/id #uuid "f97fbfa3-2919-5c1f-9f3e-cfe50f54bc39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279386} {:answer/id #uuid "fd778905-d531-5c6c-8fec-23c7b781c07e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6181be44-4b76-5745-86b9-4ac35f4a7823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279384} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f4d6feb-9da3-537c-9629-0de0aafa5857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "336b79c5-18db-552d-b951-bcb2a0206897" :question/math-academy-id "q-42800" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8})=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +2n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{24}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{12}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279388 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0e3c71f-a4eb-5697-9a02-b66d9f85421c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279390} {:answer/id #uuid "537d4e14-d95d-53db-a43d-2601816e536c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279391} {:answer/id #uuid "3f40e1f4-6d41-59f8-bf01-021e79ceab9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279392} {:answer/id #uuid "1c2ea7f8-8be8-55d5-8f36-4a20fd925067" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279393} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a47d39-0b41-5176-af76-af7ca7749ddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f40e1f4-6d41-59f8-bf01-021e79ceab9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279392} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4f91f24-660b-5989-8461-574ba0cf2e00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10102690-223d-5bcf-a385-350cb050888e" :question/math-academy-id "q-65848" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=b\\pi +2n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $b?$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi , & \\, & \\, & x+\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}]}
